{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/866133-will-there-be-a-book-about-infrastructures","id":866133,"title":"Will there be a book about infrastructures ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-15T14:55:17-07:00","id":866133,"title":"Will there be a book about infrastructures ?","content":"I wanted to know will there be a book that will cover infrastructures ?<br /> <br /> You can have a chapter that shows different infrastructures from around the world. Also seed idea for infrastructures and the systems that support it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T13:57:21-07:00","id":866512,"title":"","content":"Alas, I don't think that's going to happen, at least not in this edition. Which is a shame, because its another thing that Demon could sorely use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:08:33-07:00","id":866517,"title":"","content":"Even just a free PDF would be invaluable. Just lists of different Infrastructure. If they're not, we could just start a thread for it, if it's not already been done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:50:37-07:00","id":866532,"title":"","content":"Indeed, even some developer commentary on Infrastructure would be useful. I know that &quot;Infrastructure&quot; is the catch-all term for anything that supports the G-M's goals, but examples, hows, and whys would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T15:40:31-07:00","id":866547,"title":"","content":"I mean, there's a whole section with sample Infrastructure in <i>Flowers of Hell</i> so I think they kind of did that already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T16:44:20-07:00","id":866566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/866133-will-there-be-a-book-about-infrastructures?p=866547#post866547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there's a whole section with sample Infrastructure in <i>Flowers of Hell</i> so I think they kind of did that already.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, not to say that it isn't a well written little section or nothing, but aside from the rather specific info on Subborning the Infrastructure that discussion consisted of six pages of general info and examples of Infrastructure. And again, not for nothing, but six pages didn't satisfy my desire for fluff or crunch on this topic, and definitely didn't answer all my questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T17:36:04-07:00","id":867202,"title":"","content":"I'd love to write something like that. Maybe it'll get included as a long section if a Night Horrors supplement for Demon gets green lighted.<br /> <br /> If that hypothetical circumstance should become reality, what kinds of questions would you like for it to answer? Or are you more interested in crap tons of examples of projects - their Infrastructure, defenses, linchpins, and outputs?<br /> <br /> The Demon sections in Dark Eras have a goodly number of examples of Infrastructure that makes them worth raiding. I also found the SCP wiki useful when initially brainstorming the Infrastructure in the little &quot;demons talk about why they Fell&quot; fiction bits at the beginning of the Demon core - not so much in the sense of stealing the ideas as seeking inspiration for how to create a high weirdness story in 300 words or less such that there *are* answers, but those answers raise even more questions. &quot;The scale model of the city can change the city's future, sure, but what does the God-Machine intend to change by using it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:57:28-07:00","id":867305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/866133-will-there-be-a-book-about-infrastructures?p=867202#post867202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to write something like that. Maybe it'll get included as a long section if a Night Horrors supplement for Demon gets green lighted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be useful to ask &quot;Who do we need to petition for Night Horrors: Demon?&quot; at this point?<br /> <br /> No, no probably not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T20:40:16-07:00","id":867331,"title":"","content":"Besides the Core, Flowers Of Hell and the ST's Guide, you have the Tales Of The God-Machine from pages 196 to 237 of CoD. I second Eric Zawadzki's suggestion of looking at the SCP Foundation wiki for inspiration. There are also threads for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/111448-01000111-01101111-01100100-plot-hooks\"><b>Plot Hooks</b></a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/770408-where-is-the-infrastructure-in-your-neighborhood\"><b>Infrastructures that might exist near you.</b></a><br /> <br /> That being said, more examples would be excellent. A Night Horrors book would be perfect for this. I'm particularly curious about Rank 6+ Angels and Cryptids, and what might happen if they Fall or enter our realm. Arch-Demons who reached their Hells would also be very interesting (especially if they want to expand and incorporate other Hells, with the PCs being seen as pawns or obstacles).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T20:56:19-07:00","id":867344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/866133-will-there-be-a-book-about-infrastructures?p=867202#post867202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to write something like that. Maybe it'll get included as a long section if a Night Horrors supplement for Demon gets green lighted.<br /> <br /> If that hypothetical circumstance should become reality, what kinds of questions would you like for it to answer? Or are you more interested in crap tons of examples of projects - their Infrastructure, defenses, linchpins, and outputs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in an Infrastructure toolkit, like the core Horror system but for Infrastructure. Also more examples, also maybe examples of building an infrastructure system. Inputs to outputs and all that.<br /> <br /> In some of the weirder infrastructures it'd be cool to have an answer to &quot;Why&quot;. Doesn't have to be a why does the GM exist, it can lead to more questions. I feel like when I'm creating infrastructure I have no idea why it exists. In some cases I feel like it's unclear how or when the GM is actually making use of something. Like the couch in the Diner in core, so people stumble onto it... but when does the GM actually use it? I find it harder to build infrastructure because I don't have answers to any of the whys. A lot of infrastructure seems to exist in a void. I get that that's the point but a little view into it would be nice.<br /> <br /> I'd be ok with say, an example infrastructure pipeline that at the end said had a why section with multiple answers kind of like the answers to &quot;what is the GM&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 04-18-2016, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T20:54:40-07:00","id":868145,"title":"","content":"noticing that I said something that by itself doesn't make much sense, when talking about an infrastructure pipeline or infrastructure system. I mean, for example if you have a city with various infrastructures that work together, it'd be nice to understand how they're working together and why the system has been set up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T21:02:34-07:00","id":868149,"title":"","content":"Actually there were a lot of calls for a &quot;Damnation City&quot; for other splats, but it occurs to me that it might be interesting to have a Gears of the Machine that was about planning a city from the perspective of the God Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T14:06:41-07:00","id":868743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/866133-will-there-be-a-book-about-infrastructures?p=867202#post867202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to write something like that. Maybe it'll get included as a long section if a Night Horrors supplement for Demon gets green lighted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also thought the Night Horrors book should have a section full of Infrastructure/occult matrices. It just makes sense to me, as they\u2019re arguably better long-term antagonists than the average angel (who is a cog in such a system).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/866133-will-there-be-a-book-about-infrastructures?p=867344#post867344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be interested in an Infrastructure toolkit, like the core Horror system but for Infrastructure. Also more examples, also maybe examples of building an infrastructure system. Inputs to outputs and all that.<br /> <br /> In some of the weirder infrastructures it'd be cool to have an answer to &quot;Why&quot;. Doesn't have to be a why does the GM exist, it can lead to more questions. I feel like when I'm creating infrastructure I have no idea why it exists. In some cases I feel like it's unclear how or when the GM is actually making use of something. Like the couch in the Diner in core, so people stumble onto it... but when does the GM actually use it? I find it harder to build infrastructure because I don't have answers to any of the whys. A lot of infrastructure seems to exist in a void. I get that that's the point but a little view into it would be nice.<br /> <br /> I'd be ok with say, an example infrastructure pipeline that at the end said had a why section with multiple answers kind of like the answers to &quot;what is the GM&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m intrigued by the idea of a toolkit, Horror-like approach, though I think it would be tricky, because Infrastructure is weird and fundamentally it has few traits: what shape it takes, what protection it has, intended outputs and how you could hack it. The coach is, in many ways, a bad example \u2018cause it\u2019s a plot device to facilitate a time travel plot. Compare it the library in Flowers of Hell or, well, anything from the Aztec Demon chapter. Those examples have a clear purpose (even if it\u2019s wonderfully crazy, like make scorpions intelligent) and even suggestions on how to hack it. The Aztec examples are really fantastic because without context they\u2019re as odd as the couch, but in context they work very well.<br /> <br /> Actually, here's a quick and dirty explanation for the couch. It's similar, though much smaller, device to the \u2018alternate timeline crumple-zone\u2019 Infrastructure beneath the Golden Gate in Istanbul. Using it for time travel is actually a hack, an unintended application.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/866133-will-there-be-a-book-about-infrastructures?p=867305#post867305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it be useful to ask &quot;Who do we need to petition for Night Horrors: Demon?&quot; at this point?<br /> <br /> No, no probably not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's your desired output. Of course, summoning such a powerful book requires a puissant occult matrix<br /> <br /> There is a secret place, in your city. <i>All </i>of your cities. Find the door with the circuitboard-skull and knock three times. The first time, there will be no answer, nor the second. On the fourth attempt something will knock back. Whisper a secret that you have never shared to that door and it will open. Do not look at the face of the man who opens it. He will give you a phone, slick with oil and blood, and at precisely 4.44 the next morning that phone will ring. Pick it up, but say nothing. Something that speaks with your voice will give you a task.Complete it, and we will be one step closer to Night Horrors: Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T22:33:53-07:00","id":869117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/866133-will-there-be-a-book-about-infrastructures?p=868743#post868743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a secret place, in your city. <i>All </i>of your cities. Find the door with the circuitboard-skull and knock three times. The first time, there will be no answer, nor the second. On the fourth attempt something will knock back. Whisper a secret that you have never shared to that door and it will open. Do not look at the face of the man who opens it. He will give you a phone, slick with oil and blood, and at precisely 4.44 the next morning that phone will ring. Pick it up, but say nothing. Something that speaks with your voice will give you a task.Complete it, and we will be one step closer to Night Horrors: Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}